    "posts": [
      {
        "id": 27512171,
        "name": null,
        "username": "Tisuri-mankrik",
        "avatar_template": "https://render.worldofwarcraft.com/classic-us/character/mankrik/116/96486516-avatar.jpg?alt=/wow/static/images/2d/avatar/5-1.jpg",
        "created_at": "2025-08-18T17:18:47.157Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I was having trouble with my Ghostclaw Lynx’s action bar. The cat’s skills (Dash, Heart of the Phoenix  Growl, Rabid, Claw, Prowl, Roar of Courage, etc) would vanish off the bar whenever I would mount up, unmount, phase, summon, dismiss. Which is a big deal because I need to be able to use Prowl properly without opening the spell book and manually toggling it or having to drag it onto my bar all the time that it resets. The game wouldn’t save my pet’s skill placements.</p>\n<p>This is when I opened a ticket.</p>\n<p>I explained my issue and got a quick and very terse ‘your pet will vanish when you mount up’ Ok. Dismissive; but it was snarky enough that a human wrote it; without any of the usual roleplay fluff that you get from opening a ticket or reporting a bug.</p>\n<p>I restated my issue with more detail and clearer language and waited 2 days. All of my previous tickets I was able to interact with the GM and have a back and forth and properly explain my issue. But this time it went right to ‘You have a message’ instead of giving me any interaction. And when I opened the ticket; I got a very… unusual response from what was clearly ChatGPT.</p>\n<p>I’ve been playing with LLM’s since AI Dungeon 2; so I have a lot of experiences with the quirks and writing slop. The GM’s post was riddled with M-Dashes (These — things) and even weirder was a multiple links that lead to nowhere and forum topics that don’t exist. That’s when I knew 100% that I was no longer talking to a person.</p>\n<p>I did eventually just abandon my pet and had to tame a new one in order to have normal pet functionality.</p>\n<p>I don’t know if I can reproduce it or if the bug was fixed but I can’t recommend any Ghostclaw Lynx pets. I don’t know how to reproduce the ChatGPT Game Master because I currently don’t have a ticket open and I’m not going to go bug hunting to get a canned response.</p>",
